# sttp

[Harman's site](https://hrmnjt.dev) — secure thought transfer protocol.
A small personal site built with Hugo: shards, builds, a write-ahead log,
and one readme. System monospace, Gruvbox, and a few useful sketches.
The catalog interleaves content in date order. Article images open in a small,
self-hosted modal viewer; original links still work without JavaScript.

## Run locally

Use Hugo Extended 0.167.0 (the version pinned in CI). Python 3.11+ is needed
only for the repository tests. The site itself needs no Node dependencies or
downloaded fonts. Optional screenshot tooling needs Node 20+ and Chromium.

    hugo server

To see design-only draft WAL entries:

    hugo server --buildDrafts

Never publish a draft-enabled build.

## Build and check

    hugo --panicOnWarning --printPathWarnings
    python3 -m unittest discover -s tests

Hugo generates `public/`; generated output and resource caches are ignored.
Tests build isolated temporary copies, including draft previews and fixtures.
CI also checks generated local links with Lychee.

## Screenshot feedback loop

On your Mac (or supported Ubuntu host), install the development-only tooling:

    npm ci
    npx playwright install chromium

Then capture a normal preview, or opt into design drafts:

    npm run screenshots
    npm run screenshots -- --drafts

The runner starts its own Hugo server on loopback port 1314, captures 24 PNGs
at desktop (1440×1000) and phone (390×844) sizes, and shuts everything down.
It never reuses your existing `hugo server`. If the port is busy:

    npm run screenshots -- --port 1320

Files are written to `.artifacts/screenshots/normal/` or `drafts/`, including
`report.md`, `report.json`, and `server.log`. These and `node_modules/` are
ignored by Git. Read the report, then share selected PNGs with the coding
session for visual review. Re-run after edits; no pixel-diff baseline is required.
The runner fails on page overflow, broken requests/images, browser errors,
or missing capture regions, while retaining screenshots for inspection.

    npm run test:screenshots
    npm run test:images

The image-viewer tests need an installed Chromium browser. They check the deployed
CSP, keyboard/touch dismissal, actual-size scrolling, focus/position restoration,
and no-JavaScript fallback.

Runner tests require no browser installation; they include a real Hugo server
smoke check when Hugo is available. `npm run screenshots -- --help` lists the
options. Playwright's bundled
browsers do not support Alpine Linux; run captures on your Mac or a supported
Linux host. Browser packages are never part of the deployed site.

## Where things live

- `content/shards/`: dated Markdown writing; URLs retain year/month/day/slug.
- `content/builds/`: build pages, with their own date and repository link.
- `content/wal/`: short dated entries, readable in full on the log page.
- `content/readme/_index.md`: the site's single context document.
- `assets/`: fingerprinted CSS, image-viewer JavaScript, images, and section sketches.
- `layouts/`: Hugo templates, Markdown hooks, and shortcodes.
- `static/`: favicons and Cloudflare Pages header configuration.
- `scripts/screenshots.mjs`: optional browser capture runner.

Use explicit titles and content dates, not automatic Git timestamps. A build
page's date is not the linked shard's date. Keep substantive revisions in
`lastmod`; catalog chronology uses the original `date`. Review draft samples
and personal copy before publishing.

## Design notes

System monospace and Gruvbox dark throughout; `assets/css/main.css` names the
palette (`--gb-*`) and assigns roles from it. Every page shares one 1100px frame
and one left rail, with prose capped at 70ch.

Each content kind is one colour, one glyph, and one lowercase name, always used
together:

| kind   | colour          | glyph                         |
| ------ | --------------- | ----------------------------- |
| shard  | Gruvbox purple  | faceted fragment              |
| build  | Gruvbox blue    | cube                          |
| wal    | Gruvbox orange  | ledger page                   |
| readme | neutral         | page with a folded corner     |

Green is reserved for links. The glyphs in `layouts/partials/kind-mark.html`
reuse the outlines of the section sketches in `assets/images/doodles/`. The
sketches themselves stay tan with green accents; only glyphs and labels take a
kind's colour. Catalog rows, article date lines, and backlink headings carry it.

Shards and builds link to each other with front-matter lists of content paths:

    related_shards = ["/shards/2026-02-01-dev"]
    related_builds = ["/builds/dev"]

Each page's "backlinks" section shows the pages it names and the pages that
name it. Unresolved, mistyped, or self-referencing entries fail the build.

## Deployment

Cloudflare Pages builds with plain `hugo` and publishes `public/`. The base
URL comes from `hugo.toml` (`https://hrmnjt.dev`), not `$CF_PAGES_URL`.
The GitHub Actions workflow checks builds; it does not deploy the site.
Verify headers and canonical/feed URLs on the deployed release.

